NAME
    coverage - query, build, and load the test coverage map

SYNOPSIS
    coverage [FILE...]
    coverage run --bin DIR [--tree DIR] [--jobs N] [--rev REV]
                 [--class C]... [--by-case C]... [--nightly]
                 [--out DIR] [--repo DIR]
    coverage load [--merge] [FILE]

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.testing module managing the source-to-test
    coverage map read by impact(1)'s 'covered' rule. For each test class
    in a .NET test project, the map records the C# source files executed
    by that class (repository paths, plus 'lunap:<path>' for sibling
    LunaP files).

    With no subcommand and no FILE arguments, prints a one-line summary
    of the map in the store (revision, build timestamp, class and file
    counts, and classes without a report). With FILE arguments, prints
    tab-separated 'FILE  UNIT' lines for each unit that executed FILE,
    or 'FILE  unseen' if the map has no record for it.

    'coverage run' executes each land-tier test class in an isolated
    dotnet test process under coverlet (excluding Category=nightly
    unless --nightly is given). Each worker runs from a private copy of
    --bin (removed on completion) with MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1 and
    UseSharedCompilation=false, and subtracts a two-run empty-filter
    xunit discovery baseline so discovery-only hits are excluded. Output
    lines stream as classes finish:

        # coverage 1  rev R  built T  bin DIR  jobs N  classes C  groups G
        # baseline  N files  M lines  SECONDS
        covered  UNIT  FILE
        ran      UNIT  SECONDS  RESULT  N files
        none     UNIT  why
        # done   N with a report, M without

    Classes that exit without producing a report are recorded under '*'
    so impact(1) selects them conservatively for any covered change.

    'coverage load' ingests a run's output from FILE or standard input
    into the testing store as a single 'coverage' trial, replacing the
    previous map atomically.

OPTIONS
    --bin DIR
        (run, required) Build output directory of the test project.
    --tree DIR
        (run) Source checkout matching the PDB paths in --bin (default:
        repository root).
    --jobs N
        (run) Number of concurrent dotnet test workers (default: 4).
    --rev REV
        (run) Git revision recorded with the map (default: HEAD).
    --class C
        (run, repeatable) Limit execution to classes whose name contains
        C.
    --by-case C
        (run, repeatable) Map matching classes per case group
        (CLASS#KEY) grouped by the first quoted display-name argument
        (minus trailing -WxH size suffixes), against a discovery-
        enumerated baseline.
    --nightly
        (run) Include nightly-tier classes.
    --out DIR
        (run) Output directory for logs and per-class reports (default:
        ~/.cache/emusen/testing/coverage).
    --repo DIR
        (run) Git repository root (overrides EMUSEN_REPO).
    --merge
        (load) Replace only rows for classes present in the incoming run
        (must match the stored map's revision).

EXAMPLES
    coverage
    coverage Platform/galaxia/src/tree.rs
    coverage run --bin EmuSen.WiseMan/bin/Debug/net10.0 --jobs 4 > map.txt
    coverage load map.txt
    coverage run --bin EmuSen.WiseMan/bin/Debug/net10.0 --class GalaxiaScopeTests --jobs 1

EXIT STATUS
    0   Map queried, built with zero missing reports, or loaded.
    1   No map in store (query mode), or one or more classes produced no
        report (run mode).
    2   Invalid options, missing files, or runtime error.

SEE ALSO
    impact(1), shard(1), trial(1), units(1)
